Fix Qt6 headers, bindings, CLI ranges, lockers and concurrent member calls.

Qt6 declares QStringList as a QList alias, so include its public declaration
instead of forward-declaring a class.  Include QEnterEvent where the existing
QtCompat alias needs it.  Pass the same build number to both standalone
Shiboken parsers as the C++ targets via --clang-option (bare -D arguments are
not accepted by Shiboken6); do not alter the exposed version method.
Include QCursor directly for the GUI manager's by-value cursor fields rather
than depending on transitive Qt headers.
Use the supported PySequence generator type in the Engine render and GUI
renderBlocking bindings while retaining the wrappers' explicit list checks.
Correct the bundled HTTP property's declared type to
match its existing accessor.  The CLI range expression remains a whole-string
match (including the empty string), not a substring search.
Deduce concrete QMutex/QRecursiveMutex locker types on Qt5 and Qt6, keeping
render lock owners in the enclosing scope through rendering and GL attach/detach.
Cast the QChar code unit to uint before passing it to QString::arg so the
integral overload is selected on Qt 6.9 (where char16_t is excluded), keeping
the same 4-digit hexadecimal \u escaping semantics.
Parse the existing Natron/Qt headers before Xlib defines Status and Bool;
retain the X11 macro environment for the platform implementation.
Use lambdas for QtConcurrent member calls on Qt5.15 and Qt6, retaining raw
target pointers, value-copied arguments and the existing watcher plumbing.
Extract the key from Qt6's QKeyCombination after the existing modifier parsing,
preserving the separate modifier result and the Qt5 integer extraction.
Replace deprecated Qt::Modifier/Qt::Key operator+ shortcut arithmetic with
bitwise OR composition (int-cast where Qt6 requires a combined-int
QKeySequence), preserving each sequence's key as the last operand.

Upstream: Qt6 portability for pinned 3763d805d7d277d10af10025ae41af677682b3e6.

